ChatGPT said:
The error occurs because Git is trying to add a Visual Studio cache file inside the .vs folder, but Windows is denying access to it. You should exclude .vs from Git because it contains local Visual Studio workspace/cache files that generally shouldn't be committed.

Step 1: Create or update .gitignore
In your project root (Inventory_Management_System), run:

bash
echo .vs/ >> .gitignore
This tells Git to ignore the .vs folder.

Step 2: Remove .vs from Git's index (if necessary)
Run:

bash
git rm -r --cached .vs
If Git says the pathspec did not match any files, you can ignore that message; it means .vs isn't currently tracked.

Step 3: Add your files again
bash
git add .
git status
Then commit your changes:

bash
git commit -m "Add inventory management system files"
Step 4: Verify your .gitignore
Your .gitignore should include something like:

gitignore
# Visual Studio
.vs/

# Build output
bin/
obj/

# User-specific files
*.user
*.suo
Why this works: Git will skip the .vs cache files, avoiding the permission error and preventing unnecessary Visual Studio files from being committed.

You generally don't need to change Windows permissions or delete the .vs folder.


